  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "The electronic configuration of Uranium is,<br /><math><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mn>5</mn><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mn>6</mn><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mn>7</mn><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math><br /><br />Hence, the maximum electrons it can lose is <math><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math> (Inner electrons do not come out due to stability)<br /><br />The electronic configuration of plutonium is,&nbsp;<math><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mn>5</mn><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mn>7</mn><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math><br /><br />It&nbsp;exhibits a maximum oxidation state of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></math>.",
